\title{monitoraSom: automated sound detection in passive acoustic monitoring}
\description{
monitoraSom matches animal-vocalization templates against long soundscape
recordings, segments regions of interest (ROIs), validates detections, and
diagnoses template performance. The workflow is: set up a workspace
(\code{\link[=set_workspace]{set_workspace()}}), segment ROIs (\code{\link[=launch_segmentation_app]{launch_segmentation_app()}}), cut
templates (\code{\link[=export_templates]{export_templates()}}), read inputs
(\code{\link[=fetch_soundscape_metadata]{fetch_soundscape_metadata()}}, \code{\link[=fetch_template_metadata]{fetch_template_metadata()}}), build the
search grid (\code{\link[=fetch_match_grid]{fetch_match_grid()}}), match (\code{\link[=run_matching]{run_matching()}} /
\code{\link[=template_matching]{template_matching()}}), validate (\code{\link[=validate_by_overlap]{validate_by_overlap()}}) and diagnose
(\code{\link[=diagnostic_validations]{diagnostic_validations()}}).
}
\section{What changed in the refactored version (before vs after 1.2.0)}{

The refactored package (the analysis flow from before monitoraSom 1.2.0
onward) keeps the same steps but reorganized the internals. Compatibility
shims keep old scripts running where it matters: \code{\link[=export_roi_cuts]{export_roi_cuts()}} is a
deprecated alias of \code{\link[=export_templates]{export_templates()}} (the \verb{roi_cuts/} folder became
\verb{templates/}, CRAN item 3); old folder names (\code{match_grid_metadata},
\code{validation_outputs}, \code{validation_diagnostics}) became \code{grids},
\code{validations} and \code{diagnostics} (\code{\link[=set_workspace]{set_workspace()}} still documents the
mapping); legacy CSV detections are still read, with a deprecation warning,
and the migration path to the signals store is documented in
\code{\link[=launch_validation_app]{launch_validation_app()}}. ROIs and detections now live together in one
\code{signals} database; the promotion of a validated detection to a ROI is
